In this episode we build a ComfyUI text to image workflow completely from scratch — every node, every connection, every decision explained as we go. No presets. No copy-pasting someone else's JSON. Just you, a blank canvas, and a working workflow by the end.
Most ComfyUI tutorials hand you a workflow and move on. This series teaches you how diffusion models actually work at their core — so you can build anything on your own, troubleshoot your own errors, and stop being dependent on other people's setups.
By the end of this video you'll understand what every core node does, why it needs to be connected the way it is, and how text to image generation actually works under the hood.
This is Episode 1 of Build With Me — a series where we go from zero to full workflows, step by step, node by node.

🔴 WHAT YOU'LL LEARN IN THIS VIDEO
→ What ComfyUI actually is and how node-based workflows work
→ The 8 core nodes every text to image workflow needs
→ What the UNETLoader, VAELoader, and CLIPLoader do and why you need all three
→ How the KSampler works and what steps, CFG, and denoise actually control
→ How to swap between different models without rebuilding your workflow
→ Why modern models like Flux 2 Klein and Z-Image Turbo use separate loaders

